><translations></translations><inputs><input type="%s"></input></inputs><script><block s="doIf"><block s="reportVariadicEquals"><list><block var="word"/><l>child</l></list></block><script><block s="doReport"><l>children</l></block></script><list></list></block><block s="doIf"><block s="reportVariadicEquals"><list><block var="word"/><l>woman</l></list></block><script><block s="doReport"><l>women</l></block></script><list></list></block><block s="doIf"><block s="reportVariadicEquals"><list><block var="word"/><l>man</l></list></block><script><block s="doReport"><l>men</l></block></script><list></list></block><block s="doIf"><block s="reportVariadicEquals"><list><block var="word"/><l>deer</l></list></block><script><block s="doReport"><l>deer</l></block></script><list></list></block><block s="doIf"><block s="reportVariadicEquals"><list><block var="word"/><l>ox</l></list></block><script><block s="doReport"><l>oxen</l></block></script><list></list></block><block s="doIf"><block s="reportVariadicEquals"><list><block var="word"/><l>mouse</l></list></block><script><block s="doReport"><l>mice</l></block></script><list></list></block></script></block-definition><block-definition s="special case plural %&apos;word&apos;" type="predicate" category="operators"><header></header><code></code><translations></translations><inputs><input type="%s"></input></inputs><script><block s="doReport"><block s="reportListContainsItem"><block s="reportNewList"><list><l>child</l><l>man</l><l>woman</l><l>deer</l><l>ox</l><l>mouse</l></list></block><block var="word"/></block></block></script></block-definition><block-definition s="testlist" type="reporter" category="lists"><header></header><code></code><translations></translations><inputs></inputs><script><block s="doReport"><block s="reportNewList"><list><l>day</l><l>butterfly</l><l>boy</l><l>spy</l><l>witch</l><l>ash</l><l>path</l><l>laugh</l><l>moth</l><l>knife</l><l>ear muff</l><l>calf</l><l>half</l><l>man</l><l>van</l><l>French fry</l><l>eye</l><l>bulldog </l><l>child</l><l>box</l><l>ox</l><l>boss</l><l>mess</l><l>mouse</l><l>chicken</l><l>medicine</l></list></block></block></script></block-definition></blocks><primitives></primitives><stage name="Stage" width="480" height="360" costume="0" color="255,255,255,1" tempo="60" threadsafe="false" penlog="false" volume="100" pan="0" lines="round" ternary="true" hyperops="true" codify="false" inheritance="false" sublistIDs="false" id="766"><pentrails>data:image/png;base64,</pentrails><costumes><list struct="atomic" id="767"></list></costumes><sounds><list struct="atomic" id="768"></list></sounds><variables></variables><blocks></blocks><scripts></scripts><sprites select="1"><sprite name="Sprite" idx="1" x="0" y="0" heading="90" scale="1" volume="100" pan="0" rotation="1" draggable="true" costume="0" color="80,80,80,1" pen="tip" id="773"><costumes><list struct="atomic" id="774"></list></costumes><sounds><list struct="atomic" id="775"></list></sounds><blocks></blocks><variables></variables><scripts><comment x="13.333333333333343" y="10" w="366.15384615384613" collapsed="false">2.OP.4.3 does not require students to fix the problems they discover, but only to discover several problems.  Students might do this collaboratively, listing words, checking them, then sharing the results to make one large list. Some rules are subtle. For example, &quot;day&quot; just adds &quot;s,&quot; but &quot;fry&quot; drops the &quot;y&quot; and adds &quot;ies.&quot;  Here is a sample list of test words. Students&apos; lists will be different.</comment><script x="13.333333333333343" y="107.00000000000013"><block s="reportNewList"><list><l>day</l><l>butterfly</l><l>boy</l><l>spy</l><l>itch</l><l>ash</l><l>path</l><l>laugh</l><l>moth</l><l>knife</l><l>ear muff</l><l>calf</l><l>half</l><l>man</l><l>van</l><l>French fry</l><l>eye</l><l>bulldog </l><l>child</l><l>box</l><l>ox</l><l>boss</l><l>mess</l><l>mouse</l><l>chicken</l><l>medicine</l></list></block></script><comment x="13.333333333333343" y="149" w="423.8461538461538" collapsed="false">Over time, languages tend to move toward simple, regular rules. In 2016 the New York Times switched from &quot;millennia&quot; to &quot;millenniums.&quot; Students may disagree about how to form the plural of particular words but, for the purposes of learning how to get a computer to handle natural language, they may choose any spelling.&#xD;&#xD;Students don&apos;t need to deal with exceptions like &quot;ox&quot; or &quot;mouse&quot; or &quot;child&quot; or &quot;man&quot; unless they find that an interesting challenge, but they should see cases that require alternative solutions.  </comment><comment x="13.333333333333343" y="270" w="188.1538461538461" collapsed="true">2.OP.4.5.  First version of PLURAL</comment><script x="13.333333333333343" y="297.0000000000002"><custom-block s="plural %s (through 2.OP.4.5)"><l></l><comment w="90" collapsed="true">Look inside.</comment></custom-block></script><script x="13.333333333333343" y="327.0000000000001"><custom-block s="plural %s (through 2.OP.4.5)"><l>day</l></custom-block></script><script x="13.333333333333343" y="354.9999999999999"><custom-block s="plural %s (through 2.OP.4.5)"><l>boss</l></custom-block></script><script x="13.333333333333343" y="382.99999999999983"><custom-block s="plural %s (through 2.OP.4.5)"><l>medicine</l></custom-block></script><script x="13.333333333333343" y="411.0000000000003"><custom-block s="plural %s (through 2.OP.4.5)"><l>box</l></custom-block></script><comment x="13.333333333333343" y="439.00000000000006" w="266.6666666666667" collapsed="true">An alternate minimal solution with a little less code:</comment><script x="13.333333333333343" y="466.00000000000006"><block s="doIf"><block s="reportListContainsItem"><block s="reportNewList"><list><l>x</l><l>s</l></list></block><custom-block s="last letter of %txt"><block var="word"/></custom-block></block><script><block s="doReport"><block s="reportJoinWords"><list><block var="word"/><l>es</l></list></block></block></script><list></list><comment w="192.25641025641002" collapsed="false">This code works only inside the definition of the PLURAL block, not on its own.</comment></block><block s="doReport"><block s="reportJoinWords"><list><block var="word"/><l>s</l></list></block></block></script><comment x="13.333333333333343" y="696.9999999999999" w="339.1282051282051" collapsed="false">Note: Although the problem requires correct behavior only for four words, you want students to be able to move beyond solutions like the following.</comment><script x="13.333333333333343" y="757.9999999999995"><block s="doIf"><block s="reportVariadicEquals"><list><block var="word"/><l>box</l></list><comment w="400.8205128205127" collapsed="false">If you see a solution like this, affirm that it works. It is not wrong, but it is also not general. Say &quot;How can you program it so that it works for /any/ words that need es?&quot;</comment></block><script><block s="doReport"><l>boxes</l></block></script><list></list></block><block s="doIf"><block s="reportVariadicEquals"><list><block var="word"/><l>boss</l></list></block><script><block s="doReport"><l>bosses</l></block></script><list></list></block><block s="doReport"><block s="reportJoinWords"><list><block var="word"/><l>s</l></list></block></block></script><comment x="13.333333333333343" y="907.6666666666661" w="406.15384615384613" collapsed="false">For a better-than-minimal solution, it&apos;s helpful, but not required, to use a helper procedure:</comment><script x="13.333333333333343" y="956.666666666666"><custom-block s="%s ends with %s ?"><l></l><l></l><comment w="172.05128205128207" collapsed="false">(word) ends with (letters)&#xD;To see definition, edit the block.</comment></custom-block></script><script x="13.333333333333343" y="1020.666666666666"><custom-block s="%s ends with %s ?"><l>fish</l><l>h</l></custom-block></script><script x="13.333333333333343" y="1048.6666666666656"><custom-block s="%s ends with %s ?"><l>fish</l><l>sh</l></custom-block></script><comment x="13.333333333333343" y="1076.6666666666656" w="409.5384615384616" collapsed="false">See page 5 FYTD 1 for a &quot;finished&quot; thorough definition of a PLURAL block. </comment><comment x="13.333333333333343" y="568.666666666667" w="379.94871794871796" collapsed="false">2.OP.4.6: As students can see, this minimal solution works only for some test words:</comment><comment x="13.333333333333343" y="1125.6666666666665" w="356.15384615384613" collapsed="false">2.OP.4.6-7.  From experimentation, the aim is for students to see that MAP applies the function to each object in the list. In 6, it produces the plural (correct or not) of each item in the list. For 7, it joins Y to each item in the list. </comment><comment x="13.333333333333343" y="1198.666666666666" w="356.15384615384613" collapsed="false">2.OP.4.8.  From experimentation, the aim is for students to see that KEEP applies the predicate (test) to each object in the list and returns a list that contains only the items that pass the test (items for which the predicate returns TRUE). </comment><comment x="13.333333333333343" y="1283.6666666666665" w="355.3333333333333" collapsed="false">TIF A. The programming is quite similar, except that it takes a pronoun as another input. In this example, IF the pronoun is ___, JOIN all but the last two letters of the verb with the appropriate ending. As with PLURAL-H and PLURAL-Y, specialists are helpful to account for the different conjugations of differently spelled verbs. </comment><script x="19.666666666666657" y="1375.0000000000002"><custom-block s="conjugate verb (Spanish) pronoun %s verb %s"><l></l><l></l></custom-block></script><script x="15" y="621.4444444444453"><block s="reportMap"><block s="reifyReporter"><autolambda><custom-block s="plural %s (through 2.OP.4.5)"><l></l></custom-block></autolambda><list></list></block><block s="reportNewList"><list><l>day</l><l>butterfly</l><l>boy</l><l>spy</l><l>itch</l><l>ash</l><l>path</l><l>laugh</l><l>moth</l><l>knife</l><l>ear muff</l><l>calf</l><l>half</l><l>man</l><l>van</l><l>French fry</l><l>eye</l><l>bulldog </l><l>child</l><l>box</l><l>ox</l><l>boss</l><l>mess</l><l>mouse</l><l>chicken</l><l>medicine</l></list></block></block></script></scripts></sprite></sprites></stage><variables></variables></scene></scenes></project>